  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "m27-s001",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-a",
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 5540,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks everyone. Kieran will drive, this is phase one of the grid dashboard."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s002",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-e",
      "startMs": 5790,
      "endMs": 14370,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "So this is the overview. All four pilot sites, output against forecast, and alarms. Data is at most fifteen minutes old."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s003",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-b",
      "startMs": 14620,
      "endMs": 18260,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "This is exactly what I wanted. One screen."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s004",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-d",
      "startMs": 18510,
      "endMs": 24430,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The drill-down per site works too. Click a site and you get inverter-level output."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s005",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-c",
      "startMs": 24680,
      "endMs": 30220,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The nightly batch has run clean every night since we switched it on."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s006",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-b",
      "startMs": 30470,
      "endMs": 33350,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "What's the one thing that's wrong?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s007",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-e",
      "startMs": 33600,
      "endMs": 40660,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The solar output chart has a timezone offset. It's an hour off for the two southern sites."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s008",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-b",
      "startMs": 40910,
      "endMs": 44170,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Please fix that before I show anyone."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s009",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-e",
      "startMs": 44420,
      "endMs": 49200,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll fix the timezone offset on the output chart by Friday."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s010",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-a",
      "startMs": 49450,
      "endMs": 51950,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Garnet, what about phase two?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s011",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-b",
      "startMs": 52200,
      "endMs": 58500,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Weather. Isolde was right in March, cloud cover explains most of the dips we chase."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s012",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-d",
      "startMs": 58750,
      "endMs": 63910,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'd add a weather overlay to the output chart in phase two."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s013",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-b",
      "startMs": 64160,
      "endMs": 68180,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Then that's decided. Phase two adds the weather overlay."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s014",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-a",
      "startMs": 68430,
      "endMs": 71310,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Decided. Anything else for phase two?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s015",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-c",
      "startMs": 71560,
      "endMs": 76720,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Alarm routing. We should probably look into paging integration at some point."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s016",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-b",
      "startMs": 76970,
      "endMs": 79090,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Not now. Weather first."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s017",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-a",
      "startMs": 79340,
      "endMs": 83360,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Isolde, how do we learn what the operators think?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s018",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-d",
      "startMs": 83610,
      "endMs": 88010,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll collect operator feedback on phase one in three weeks."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s019",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-a",
      "startMs": 88260,
      "endMs": 89240,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Perfect."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s020",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-b",
      "startMs": 89490,
      "endMs": 91990,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Isolde, how's the MBA going?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s021",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-d",
      "startMs": 92240,
      "endMs": 97020,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Exhausting. Part-time MBA plus this is a lot, but I'm halfway."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s022",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-b",
      "startMs": 97270,
      "endMs": 99390,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "We're proud of her."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27-s023",
      "speakerId": "m27-spk-a",
      "startMs": 99640,
      "endMs": 106320,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks all. So: timezone fix by Friday, weather overlay in phase two, feedback in three weeks."
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Solvane grid dashboard phase one demo\n\n**Date:** July 9\n**Attendees:** Alma Mockwell (Larkspur Labs), Kieran Testcase (Larkspur Labs), Garnet Dummyson (Solvane Energy), Rafferty Fixture (Solvane Energy), Isolde Placeholder (Solvane Energy)\n\n## Summary\n\nKieran demonstrated phase one of the Solvane Energy grid dashboard. Garnet confirmed it delivers what she asked for: one screen for every pilot site.\n\n## What was shown\n\n- An overview of all four pilot sites showing output against forecast and alarms, with data at most fifteen minutes old.\n- A per-site drill-down to inverter-level output.\n- The nightly batch has run cleanly every night since it was switched on.\n\n## Issues\n\n- The solar output chart has a timezone offset, an hour off for the two southern sites. Garnet wants it fixed before she shows the dashboard to anyone.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- **Phase two adds a weather overlay** to the output chart. Garnet noted Isolde was right in March: cloud cover explains most of the dips the team chases.\n- Alarm paging integration is not in phase two; weather comes first.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Kieran Testcase** — fix the timezone offset on the output chart by Friday.\n- **Isolde Placeholder** — collect operator feedback on phase one in three weeks.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Isolde is halfway through a part-time MBA.\n- Rafferty raised paging integration as something to look into at some point; nobody took it on.\n"
  },
